                <pb facs="0334" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4812: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-08T11:00:00+03:00">July 8, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>459. Legation’s 455, July 6. No trains have arrived or left since July 5th. I am
                    reliably though not officially informed that about 3 kilometers of the railway
                    line were destroyed by an Abyssinian band this side of Mojo and killing Italian
                    guard of 40 men at Addas some 25 miles from here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
